mc-hdd (0.0.6-1) bullseye; urgency=medium

  * uhdd takes the reserved area of a container as eight tracks and starts a
    floppy at its directory. It used to take seven and start ten sectors before
    the directory, so every floppy but the first was handed the tail of the one
    before it in place of its eighth track.
  * uhdd hands over blocks 390 and 391, which the container holds and the DPB of
    the system counts. Files did reach them and were coming out with the tail cut
    off and no word about it; a floppy like that is now an image of 166 tracks,
    the size T72.fdd itself has.
  * uhdd refuses a file that carries no CP/M directory instead of writing it into
    the container, and never writes over the label sector of a floppy.

 -- Yauheni Kundo <e.kundo@gmail.com>  Tue, 25 Aug 2026 22:00:00 +0200

